# THE PUBLIC-REPO ALLOWLIST (the owner, 2026-10-09: "i dont want to hide anything" — and the trading code never leaves).
#
# One git pathspec per line (a file, a directory, or a glob git understands). scripts/ops/publish-public-repo.sh copies exactly the
# TRACKED files these lines match into the public tree, at the same paths, and nothing else: ignored files (data/, .next/, builds,
# local env files) can never be matched because git does not track them. This is an allowlist, never a denylist — a new private
# directory is private by default; a new public file is published only when a line here names it.
#
# A line that matches no tracked file is reported as a warning (not an error), so a renamed directory is noticed.
# config/public-repo.denypatterns is the second gate: every copied text file is scanned against it, and the check fails on a hit.

# --- the on-chain program (Anchor) and its generator scripts ---
programs/burn-receipts

# --- the TypeScript client of the program ---
src/lib/burnReceipts
scripts/burnreceipts-*.mts

# --- pair_curve (2026-10-10): its TypeScript client, admin CLI and the Squads v4 upgrade-proposal tool (the program itself is under
#     programs/burn-receipts, the same Anchor workspace) ---
src/lib/pairCurve
scripts/paircurve-*.mts
scripts/squads-program-upgrade.mts

# --- the $DEFICIT keeper (single-token) ---
src/lib/burnKeeper
config/burnkeeper
scripts/burn-keeper.mts
scripts/burnkeeper-*.mts
scripts/burnkeeper-keygen.mjs

# --- the platform (multi-token keeper, registry, oracles, token pages, trust page, launch wizard, API routes) ---
src/lib/burnticker
src/app/burnticker
src/app/api/burnticker
config/burnticker
scripts/burnticker-*.mts
# the operator statement's self-contained verifier (ops-2, 2026-10-12): no repository code, anyone can run it
scripts/burnticker-verify-statement.mjs
scripts/whitepaper-html.mjs

# --- the public SDK for bots (@burnticker/sdk) and the manifest of the repo files it imports (kept current by test/burntickerSdkLeak.test.ts;
#     every file it lists is covered by the src/lib/{burnticker,burnReceipts,burnKeeper} lines above) ---
packages/burnticker-sdk
packages/burnticker-sdk/public-closure.json
# the bot starter kit (growth batch 2026-10-10): follow / launch-preview / post-queue samples on the SDK; imports only the SDK (through
# its one line src/sdk.ts) and the public post generator + copy lint named below
packages/burnticker-bot-starter

# --- public launch content: the daily post and its copy lint (the token page and scripts/burnkeeper-post-draft.mts import them) and
